### BREAK 6 - REFUSAL: the marker is renamed
The marker is the whole coupling between the page and the gate. Renaming one
end must not leave a gate that quietly checks nothing - the empty result that
reads as clean, which this repository has been caught by twice.
-----------------------------------------------------------------
$ make page-tense-check
node scripts/check-page-tense.mjs
page-tense-check: REFUSED
expected exactly one begin marker and one end marker in site/index.html, found 1 and 0. The block this gate checks is identified by them; renaming one leaves the gate testing nothing at all.
make: *** [Makefile:300: page-tense-check] Error 1
exit=2 (make's status; the script itself exits 1)

