### BREAK 7 FAILED TO BREAK, AND THE GATE WAS RIGHT TO STAY GREEN
The reading above is not evidence that the coupling check works. Two things
were wrong with the probe, and only the first was mine:

  the check asks for AT LEAST ONE call outside the block, and the probe removed
  one of two. The re-render signature still called figuresAreOlder(), so the
  page really was still asking - green was the correct answer to the question
  actually posed

  and then, removing BOTH calls, it was STILL green. The phase header's own
  COMMENT reads "figuresAreOlder() is that question". A coupling check
  satisfied by prose about the coupling is exactly the instrument this
  repository keeps catching itself with, and it was found only because a break
  test that failed to break was pushed on instead of written up.

Fixed in scripts/check-page-tense.mjs: comments are stripped before the search.
Both probes re-run below against the fixed gate.
